<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices fall, rain seen helping crop.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices fall, rain seen helping crop.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices fell on Monday by 200-300 rupees per tonne on increasing arrivals in central region markets but rains in the same area is seen helping the crop, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were sharply down on heavy selling from processing plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent fell by 1,200 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 500 rupees, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady but rapeseed extraction was firm on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $275-276 for ready shipment and $272-273 for November, December and January new season shipments. Rapeseed extraction was $122 in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,150 rupees FOR Bedibunder and 4,100-4,125 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
